{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And when a man opens a pit.</b> That was fully finished many days ago, <b>or</b> even when a man digs a pit and does not cover it toward evening, because he wants to return the next day to his work of digging the pit." "<b>And does not cover it.</b> This teaches that if he covered it he is exempt — but specifically properly. And how much is 'properly'? Enough that a cart loaded with stones can pass over it, as stated in the Yerushalmi, chapter Hazakat ha-Batim: one may not make a hollow space beneath Rosh HaShanah unless a cart loaded with stones can pass over it." "<b>And falls there an ox.</b> And not a person, because a person is possessed of understanding and must examine and walk, and he himself destroyed himself. <b>A donkey</b> and not utensils, for it is not the way of utensils to be moved about without a person guarding them, and since he did not guard them, he himself destroyed them. Another interpretation: <b>an ox or a donkey</b> — the same law applies to other animals, but these are specified because their way is to go without a driver."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:40.368030262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}